# Testing

Use Vitest. Unit-test business logic in `modules/` and `lib/`, not UI-only happy paths. Colocate as `modules/<domain>/*.test.ts` or `tests/<domain>.test.ts`. Import `describe` / `it` / `expect` from `vitest`. No `any`.

If `vitest.config.mts` or `npm test` is missing, add a minimal node-env config (include `tests/**/*.test.ts`, `modules/**/*.test.ts`, `lib/**/*.test.ts`) and `"test": "vitest run"`. Do not write the whole CRM suite.

Mock Stripe, R2, and Resend. Do **not** mock away the rule under test (tenant `where`, accept transaction, webhook idempotency).

```ts
// ❌ BAD — id-only fetch; mocks the invariant
prisma.bidRequest.findUnique({ where: { id } })
vi.mocked(acceptBid).mockResolvedValue(winner)

// ✅ GOOD — tenant scope + real service
prisma.bidRequest.findFirst({ where: { id, organizationId: ctx.organizationId } })
await expect(acceptBid(ctxB, { bidId })).rejects.toThrow(ConflictError)
```

## Must cover (when that module exists)

| Area | Assert |
| --- | --- |
| Authz | missing permission → `AuthorizationError` |
| Tenant | org A id cannot be read/updated as org B |
| Lead conversion | transaction creates client/opportunity; rollback on failure |
| Proposal accept | status + optional project create |
| Bid submit | closed request rejected; duplicate active bid rejected |
| Bid negotiate | original amount unchanged; history appended |
| Bid accept | one winner; others rejected; request AWARDED |
| Concurrent accept | second transaction fails; still one winner |
| Invoice math | totals, amountDue, paid-cannot-exceed-total |
| Stripe webhook | signature required; duplicate `providerPaymentId` / event id → no duplicate payment |
| Profit | `revenue - resourceCost - expenses - paymentFees`; revenue 0 → `—` (no NaN) |

## Commands

Targeted: `npx vitest run path/to/file.test.ts`. Then `npm test`, `npm run typecheck`, `npm run lint`. Use `npm run build` before deploy / Phase 12 — not after every unit test.

E2E (Playwright later, Phase 12): login → lead → convert → opportunity → proposal → accept → project → bid → negotiate → accept → invoice → webhook → profit.

Do not add snapshot-heavy UI tests for every form.
